Content Notice
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The Bhagavad Gita text is an ancient scripture and is in the public domain.
Translations and commentaries included in this project are sourced from
public-domain works and freely-licensed academic resources, including:

  • Swami Sivananda's translation and commentary (Divine Life Society)
  • A.C. Bhaktivedanta Swami Prabhupada's translation (fetched from vedabase.io
    in accordance with their terms for non-commercial educational use)
  • Adi Shankaracharya's commentary (ancient text, public domain)
  • Sri Aurobindo's essays on the Gita (Sri Aurobindo Ashram, open access)
  • IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite data (open academic resource)

This application does not claim authorship over any translated or commentary
text. All credit belongs to the respective authors and publishers. No
copyrighted material is redistributed without permission.
